---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const editor = 'https://app.pagescms.org/';
const actions = 'https://github.com/sinashiry/sinashiry.github.io/actions';
---
<Base title="Edit this website — Sina Shiri" description="Entrance to the Pages CMS editor for sina-shiri.com." noindex><div class="wrap"><section class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">WEBSITE EDITOR</span><h1>Edit this<br />website.</h1><p>Text, CVs, blog posts and papers are edited in Pages CMS, a separate editing service. This page only links to it: GitHub and Pages CMS decide who may edit.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={editor} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Pages CMS ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href={actions} rel="noopener noreferrer">Deploy status ↗</a></div></section><article class="prose" style="padding-bottom:85px"><h2>Make a change</h2><ol><li>Open <a href={editor} rel="noopener noreferrer">Pages CMS</a> and sign in with the <strong>sinashiry</strong> GitHub account.</li><li>The first time only: when Pages CMS asks, install its GitHub app and choose <strong>Only select repositories</strong> and <strong>sinashiry.github.io</strong>.</li><li>Open <strong>sinashiry / sinashiry.github.io</strong> on the <strong>main</strong> branch and pick a section in the sidebar.</li><li>Edit the text and select <strong>Save</strong>. Saving publishes: the website updates once the automatic checks and build finish, usually within a few minutes.</li><li>If a check fails, the website stays as it was. The deploy status page names the field to correct; fix it in Pages CMS and save again.</li></ol><h2>What is public</h2><p>The website’s source is a public GitHub repository. Everything saved in Pages CMS, including drafts, unapproved recommendations, referee details and uploaded files, is visible there with its full history as soon as it is saved, even before it appears on the website. Save only what may be public.</p><h2>Deploy status</h2><p>Every save starts a deploy. Its progress and any error messages appear on the repository’s <a href={actions} rel="noopener noreferrer">Actions tab</a>.</p><h2>Undo a change</h2><p>Each save is kept in the repository history. To go back, copy the earlier text into Pages CMS and save, or ask the maintainer to revert the change.</p></article></div></Base>
